    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0309" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.51 D 481/29</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Secretary handed me back the attached papers this afternoon and informed me
                    that this matter of the potash loan had been discussed with the President and
                    Mr. Mellon (Mr. Hoover being absent), at Cabinet this morning. In the
                    circumstances, it was decided that our policy should remain unchanged.</p>
                <p>By direction of the Secretary, I telephoned Mr. Jerome D. Greene, of Lee,
                    Higginson and Company, that our policy remains unchanged. Mr. Greene stated that
                    he regretted that this was so.</p>
                <p>All the papers may now go to IB for indexing and file.</p>
                <closer><signed>L[<hi rendition="#small-caps">eland</hi>] H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">arrison</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
